OPEN CAVEAT (per ticket's flagged analytical question, HONEST REPORT, not glossed
over): `adb shell input tap` on this device pool does NOT route through TalkBack's
own touch-exploration/double-tap-to-activate gesture pipeline — independently
confirmed live in this same session: a raw tap-then-tap (both a slow and a
same-shell-invocation back-to-back pair) at a native Android permission dialog's
button, with TalkBack fully bound, produced ZERO `SpeechControllerImpl: Speaking
fragment` lines in `adb logcat` (the NEARS-2315-established live-utterance signal)
and did NOT dismiss the dialog — i.e. touch exploration never even registered the
synthetic tap as an explore gesture on this pool. This is a pre-existing, already-
documented tooling limitation (docs/data-qa/verification-checks.md §"What does NOT
work on this pool"), not something newly broken by this fix, and it applied
EQUALLY to the ORIGINAL NEARS-1963 QA pass — neither run could drive a genuine
TalkBack double-tap gesture via adb on this pool. So: what's confirmed here is
that the SAME raw-coordinate-tap proxy the original matrix used (in both rows)
now succeeds post-fix. What remains UNCONFIRMED by live gesture-drive (both then
and now, a pool tooling ceiling, not a fix gap) is whether TalkBack's own
distinct double-tap gesture — which Flutter's engine routes via
SemanticsAction.tap rather than raw hit-testing — independently reaches the
field. Structural evidence FOR this working: the pre-existing (NEARS-1963,
UNCHANGED by this fix) `Semantics(onTap: () => _pinFocusNode.requestFocus())`
wrapper's node carries `actions: tap` in the live semantics tree
(talkback-on-semantics-actions.txt, "Verification Code" node) — meaning a real
SemanticsAction.tap dispatch (what TalkBack's real double-tap gesture sends) DOES
reach `_pinFocusNode.requestFocus()` via a code path this fix did not touch.
This is code-structural confirmation, not a fresh live gesture-drive proof.
RECOMMENDATION: physical-device or real-TalkBack-gesture follow-up to close this
narrow residual gap — already flagged as a non-blocking followup by the ticket
brief, not a gate on this ticket.

CLEANUP: TalkBack disabled immediately after this matrix (enabled_accessibility_services
deleted, accessibility_enabled=0) per the mandatory cleanup rule — verified below.
